 ("Dermoscopy of PR.", ["Yellowish background with peripheral whitish collarette scale and dotted/ irregular vessels — helps distinguish from guttate psoriasis (uniform dotted vessels with central scale)"]),
 ("What are the features of PR in children and dark skin?", ["More papular, vesicular, inverse (face, axillae, groin), prominent post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation/ hypopigmentation, oral lesions; often itchy; may be mistaken for scabies or secondary syphilis"]),
 ("Describe PR-like drug eruptions.", ["Drugs: ACE inhibitors (captopril), gold, bismuth, isotretinoin, metronidazole, omeprazole, terbinafine, imatinib, NSAIDs, clonidine, adalimumab; vaccines (influenza, hepatitis B, COVID-19)", "Clues: no herald patch, more itch, larger lesions, eosinophils on histology, persists until drug stopped"]),
